.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt QUOTA 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm quota
.Nd show disk usage and limits
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl guqv
.Nm
.Op Fl qv
.Fl u Ar user ...
.Nm
.Op Fl qv
.Fl g Ar group ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows, for each volume with quotas, how much a user or group uses and
the limits set for it
.Pq see Xr edquota 8 :
space in 1K blocks, then files, each with its soft limit
.Pq Dq quota ,
hard limit and, past the soft limit, the time left to get back under it
.Pq Dq grace .
A
.Ql *
marks usage over a limit.
Volumes without limits for that user or group are left out.
.Pp
With no name, it shows the user running it; only the super-user may ask
about others.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl g
Groups: with no name, those of the user running it.
.It Fl u
Users (the default).
.It Fl q
Only say where usage is over a limit.
.It Fl v
Show the volumes without limits too.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
1 when some usage is over a limit, or on an error; 0 otherwise.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr quotactl 2 ,
.Xr edquota 8 ,
.Xr quotacheck 8 ,
.Xr quotaon 8 ,
.Xr repquota 8
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is its own.
